			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement vscode-webview-resource schemes and enforce COEP\n\nRegister asynchronous URI scheme handlers for `vscode-webview-resource` and `vscode-resource` to intercept legacy VS Code asset requests. These schemes are rewritten to `vscode-file://vscode-app` and forwarded to the existing `VscodeFileSchemeHandler`, compensating for the disabled service worker in the WebKit-based webview.\n\nSimultaneously, update `VscodeFileSchemeHandler` responses to include `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin` and `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp` headers. This configuration enables the COEP-isolated webview iframe to load extension assets (React bundles, CSS, fonts) without being blocked by WebKit's cross-origin security policies, ensuring extension content renders correctly.\n\nThis bridges the gap between stock VS Code's URI handling and Tauri's custom protocol implementation, restoring asset visibility for extensions like Roo and GitLens within the editor.",
			"SHA": "f65fa4338464ae53c577a5883b9256c8a26517e4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
